{"data":{"attachmentkeynames":["rs"],"desc":"\"Start a new working branch from master.\" Compound and transactional: fetch --prune -> checkout the default branch (master, else main) -> merge --ff-only origin/<default> (a diverged local default is an error to see, never papered over) -> checkout -b <branch> -> push -u origin <branch>. Cuts from the REMOTE's default, never from wherever HEAD is, so an abandoned branch cannot leak into the next one; publishes at birth so the sweeper can push from the first commit. Requires a clean tree unless you are ON the default branch, in which case uncommitted edits ride into the new branch (the 'edited on master by mistake' rescue; reported as carried). Refuses an existing branch name, the default branch name, or a merge in flight. Returns {status, msg, branch, default, base (short sha), fetched, published, publish_err, carried, steps}.","import":"use ndata::dataarray::DataArray;","params":[{"name":"repo","type":"String"},{"name":"branch","type":"String"}],"returntype":"FLAT","type":"rust"},"id":"ymlwwx1a0733d3513t9","readers":[],"time":1788639893937,"username":"system","writers":[]}